  "about_bioClose": "Different domains, same delivery: the entire mobile front end — and, when the project calls for it, hands-on work on back ends, BFFs and web front ends.",
  "delivery_entrega_eyebrow": "DELIVERY",
  "delivery_entrega_title": "Clear scope,",
  "delivery_entrega_titleAccent": "aligned expectations.",
  "delivery_entrega_body": "Every project starts with the cut: what's in, what's out, and how each decision ties to an acceptance criterion. Without that, sprints become deadline races. I work with PO and design from kickoff so the backlog reflects what ships — not what looks good in the prototype.",
  "delivery_craft_eyebrow": "CRAFT",
  "delivery_craft_title": "Architecture and",
  "delivery_craft_titleAccent": "sound practices.",
  "delivery_craft_body": "Explicit architecture decisions: feature-first Clean Architecture and SOLID drawing each class's boundaries. Consistent code patterns (Bloc/Cubit, repository, constructor injection) plus behavior-driven (BDD) and spec-driven (SDD) development — every feature starts with a contract and tests, not improvisation.",
  "delivery_collab_eyebrow": "COLLABORATION",
  "delivery_collab_title": "Mobile at the core,",
  "delivery_collab_titleAccent": "full stack when delivery calls for it.",
  "delivery_collab_body": "My specialty is mobile front end in Flutter, but on every team I've worked with I also contributed across the rest of the stack: back ends, BFFs and web front ends, closing deliveries end to end. On large teams I own feature scope or architecture; on small teams (B2B retail, 5 years) I led the whole app, from design to deploy.",
